## Lab vs Natural — Does It Matter for a Vintage Ring?

Here is the honest answer: it depends on why you want a vintage ring.

If you love the 1920s and want a ring that actually honors that era, go natural. An original Art Deco piece would have had a natural diamond. A GIA-certified natural asscher is the authentic choice.

If you want the vintage aesthetic at lower cost, or if you want to size up (get 1.5ct for what 1ct costs naturally), a lab diamond is practical. The stone is physically and chemically identical to natural. The setting does not know the difference.

